  "passage": {
    "text": "Farmers often need capital. In spring they buy seeds and fertilizer, but they receive income only in autumn. So they go to a bank and ask for a loan. A loan is money that you must repay later with interest. Governments also support farmers. This support is a subsidy. A farmer can get a subsidy for work that protects the environment, for example for planting flowers near the fields. Not everybody likes subsidies. Some economists say that farmers should earn money only from the market. Other people say that farmers need financial help.",
